{"id": "EUVD-2026-82229", "enisaUuid": "52c5074b-1b20-3c06-9dfc-ef2aad26e979", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_fs: Fix fence cleanup in ffs_dmabuf_transfer() error paths\n\nThe error paths for endpoint-disabled (ESHUTDOWN) and request-allocation\nfailure (ENOMEM) in ffs_dmabuf_transfer() jump to err_fence_put which\ncalls dma_fence_put() on the fence. However, at that point the fence has\nonly been kmalloc'd \u2014 dma_fence_init() has not been called yet, so the\nrefcount and the fence ops are uninitialized. Calling dma_fence_put() on\nsuch an object leads to undefined behavior.\n\nUse kfree() instead, since the fence is just a plain allocation at this\nstage, and rename the label to err_fence_free to reflect the actual\ncleanup action.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:54", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be539138d9a187af3b884525a395db10797c64f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fd8baacc7dc477df9cac61b45491840247a9b1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58952c83dfe6ea3294a74734d2d1018c1120779a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/621707dc67c9846fd876d7579ec951d92aa033f1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vg86-rjrh-q8jw", "CVE-2026-93121"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00606674-e416-3a8a-83ae-8b64ff6999b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "1a5050b5-5847-3936-a8ac-d642ce0f7929", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "426cb619-6086-3c62-b282-46c4fc355d7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b07a2a7ca02a20124b552be96c5a56910795488 <be539138d9a187af3b884525a395db10797c64f1"}, {"id": "42918512-53d2-39a9-a571-5cb8a8bd710c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b07a2a7ca02a20124b552be96c5a56910795488 <5fd8baacc7dc477df9cac61b45491840247a9b1e"}, {"id": "4bedb9b0-fb8d-3408-be36-9549921a9394", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "66558f48-e28e-3557-a2fd-74eed2d1762a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b6ebf105-26cd-33c3-b9a2-730e0e1c6011", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b07a2a7ca02a20124b552be96c5a56910795488 <621707dc67c9846fd876d7579ec951d92aa033f1"}, {"id": "be2aaa3f-9191-3b1c-b8ef-5a90ec4e830a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "c38e154a-9b89-3ee3-91e5-2ade5b22ab36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "defe317a-21b7-3473-8177-f12f1029ee06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b07a2a7ca02a20124b552be96c5a56910795488 <58952c83dfe6ea3294a74734d2d1018c1120779a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5e212cae-47fe-3d46-8cf6-ef7932564717", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}